Looking at the codebase, I can see a fully-functional single-file HTML app implementing a capybara market scanner. Let me write the distilled prompt:

---

Build BaraMarket Scanner: a single-file HTML app (index.html) that discovers and scores markets & products for capybara relevance.

## Domain & Data

Define 6 capybara interest categories with weighted keyword scoring:
- **Food & Forage**: melons, grass, hay, bamboo, corn, lettuce, carrots, vegetables, pellets
- **Habitat & Shelter**: mud, wallow, burrow, shade, hut, bedding, straw, riverbank, marsh
- **Aquatic & Swimming**: pool, pond, water, swim, float, bath, hotspring, onsen, splash, lagoon, river
- **Enrichment & Play**: toy, chew, puzzle, ball, tunnel, scratch, forage, log, rope, climb, treat
- **Grooming & Wellness**: brush, groom, fur, comb, spa, massage, dental, shampoo
- **Social & Companionship**: friend, flock, duck, bird, perch, herd, companion, chill, zen, calm

Also define anti-keywords that penalize relevance: cat, dog, leash, cage, predator, jaguar, caiman, electronics, phone.

Create 7 hardcoded market feeds (Pantanal Wholesale, Izu Onsen, Chiguiro Store, Rodent Republic, São Paulo Farmers, Zen Garden Depot, Everglade Outfitters), each with 5 sample product listings (title, description, price in capycoins).

## UI (dark theme, monospace font)

Header: capybara emoji + "BARAMARKET SCANNER v1.0" title + tagline.

Control panel: START SCAN button, min-relevance threshold dropdown (30/50/70/90%), search input, JSON/CSV export buttons, progress bar, console log output.

Stats grid: markets scanned, listings crawled, capy matches, top category.

Category filter: 6 chips (one per category), toggleable, all active by default.

Results section: market cards with product tables (title, matched keywords, category tag, price, relevance score pill). Score pills color-coded: 70%+ green, 45-69% yellow, <45% red.

## Core Features

**Scan engine**: async scan button crawls all markets sequentially with simulated per-listing delays (~60-90ms) and per-market connection delays (~220-480ms). Log real-time progress to console.

**Scoring**: for each listing, search title+description for keyword matches, sum weights by category, subtract anti-keyword penalties, clamp to 0-100%. Match if above threshold AND has a top category.

**Filtering**: results filter by active categories, min threshold, and text search (query matches product title/description/matched keywords).

**Exports**: JSON (baramarket-scan.json) and CSV (baramarket-scan.csv) with market metadata and product details.

**UI state**: search input disabled until scan completes; export buttons disabled if no matches; stats update live during scan; results sorted by relevance per market; empty state shows "🔍 waiting" or "🙈 no matches" depending on state.

